Package: ggjbrowse
Title: Genome Browser Tracks as Data Frames for 'ggplot2'
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Colin", "Diesh", email = "colindiesh@berkeley.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Reads a region of a BAM, CRAM or feature file as the 'JBrowse 2'
    genome browser draws it, through the browser's own data engine run in
    'V8': the reads on their pileup rows in the browser's colors, their
    mismatches, gaps, insertions and clips, the coverage and the splice
    junctions, or the gene models laid out on their rows with their labels,
    each as a data frame, and draws the browser's tracks with 'ggplot2'.
License: Apache License (>= 2)
URL: https://github.com/GMOD/ggjbrowse
BugReports: https://github.com/GMOD/ggjbrowse/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Imports:
    curl,
    ggplot2 (>= 4.0.0),
    grid,
    jsonlite,
    patchwork,
    scales,
    V8
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
